---
import { SOCIAL } from '../data/org';

/*
 * The trail status banner.
 *
 * The prototype shows "All trails open — 6 miles groomed" here. That is live
 * data and there is no source for it yet — where it comes from is still being
 * decided (ADR 0005, docs/plans/trail-status.md).
 *
 * So the banner holds its place and says only what is true: conditions are on
 * Facebook. A hard-coded "All trails open" would be the one failure mode that
 * actually matters here — a stale claim that the trails are open in winter is
 * worse than no claim at all.
 *
 * When the source is decided this becomes the real status, and it must carry
 * its own timestamp and expire.
 */
---

<p class="trail-status">
  <span class="trail-status__label">Trail conditions</span>
  <span>
    Posted on <a href={SOCIAL[0].href} rel="noopener">our Facebook page</a> — check there before
    heading out.
  </span>
</p>
